---
description: Keep Feynman UI copy concise, concrete, and useful; avoid decorative filler.
alwaysApply: true
---

# UI copy

- Do not add decorative subtitles, motivational taglines, cute filler, or generic personalization copy to the UI unless the user explicitly requests it.
- Avoid lines like "A few details that make this space yours," "Every good adventure starts with a name," or "A little curiosity. A place to make it grow."
- Prefer a clear heading alone when the page or control already explains itself. Do not replace removed filler with another tagline.
- Add helper text only when it explains a meaningful action, requirement, limitation, state, or consequence that is not already obvious.
- Keep necessary instructions and validation messages short, specific, and direct.
